# 2. Blocklist IP Search — Corrected and Optimized Pseudocode

## A. Corrected Algorithm: Linear Search

**Input:** Blocklist and IP address to check.

**Output:** TRUE if the IP address is blocked; otherwise FALSE.

```text
ALGORITHM CORRECTED_IS_BLOCKED(blocklist, ip)

    FOR each address IN blocklist
        IF address = ip
            RETURN TRUE
        END IF
    END FOR

    RETURN FALSE

END ALGORITHM
```

## B. Optimized Algorithm: Set Membership

```text
ALGORITHM OPTIMIZED_IS_BLOCKED(blocklist_set, ip)

    IF ip EXISTS IN blocklist_set
        RETURN TRUE
    ELSE
        RETURN FALSE
    END IF

END ALGORITHM
```

**Time Complexity:**
- Corrected linear search: O(n) per query in the worst case.
- Optimized set lookup: O(1) average per query, after building the set in O(n) time.

**Purpose:** Identify whether an IP address appears in the security blocklist. The optimized implementation builds the set once and reuses it for multiple queries.
